==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}}, late 14th century, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|indigence}} (13th century), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|indigentia}}, from {{m|la|indigentem}}, form of {{m|la|indigere||to need}}, from {{m|la|indu||in, within}} + {{m|la|egere||be in need, want}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

Only relation to antonym {{m|en|affluence}} is common Latinate suffix {{suffix|en||ence}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[extreme]] [[poverty]] or [[destitution]]

